        "A CSS class is sometimes an intentional stable contract, but a generated styling class rarely is. A test id can be a deliberate automation contract for a control with no useful semantic identifier. It does not make that control accessible. Choose between semantic locators and test ids by the behavior being protected, then document the contract with the application team."
